.\design\releases\0_2_0\card__eeb46f0d-77d7-4a9d-a83e-b64e9101b994.json:569:          "content": ".\\design\\architecture\\data_saving_and_commits.md:7:Editors update application state immediately. `CommitBatcher` later coalesces repeatable edits into durable repository writes.\n.\\design\\architecture\\data_saving_and_commits.md:14:  → CommitBatcher replaces that file's pending change\n.\\design\\architecture\\data_saving_and_commits.md:72:`SaveStateService` wraps mutating storage methods and counts active operations; `DataService` also tracks queued batches. `hasPendingSave` therefore covers queued batches, active storage calls, and unresolved action drafts.\n.\\design\\architecture\\data_saving_and_commits.md:83:Commands needing an immediate repository result bypass `CommitBatcher`: creating cards or folders, deleting files, moving release files, saving project or schedule configuration, and adding or removing Git worktrees.\n.\\design\\architecture\\current_model_react.md:14:├─ hasPendingSave: boolean\r\n.\\design\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:48:        class CommitBatcher\n.\\design\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:288:    DataService *-- CommitBatcher : owns after init\n.\\design\\releases\\0_0_2\\B_022_commit_batcher_message.md:14:`CommitBatcher.schedule` (`app/src/data/commit_batcher.ts`) overwrites `pendingMessage` on every call, so a 30-second batch touching several files (card move updates two/three files; edits across cards) is committed as \"Update {lastFile}\" — a misleading history for the repo the app is supposed to manage cleanly.\n.\\design\\activity\\project.json:1064:          \"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"conversations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"actionId\\\": \\\"5b88355d-f964-459a-bc67-6618650866ba\\\",\\n      \\\"cardInternalId\\\": \\\"16bc6dc5-0f8e-421d-b0a9-c83d3a3a65f0\\\",\\n      \\\"cardPath\\\": \\\"design/feature_descriptions/F_137_group_toolcalls.md\\\",\\n      \\\"completedAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-06T19:07:11.623Z\\\",\\n      \\\"entries\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"Add `Current state`, `implementation details`, `acceptance criteria` for `design/feature_descriptions/F_137_group_toolcalls.md`.&#x20;\\\\n\\\\nRead all referenced files before you begin except `agents` files. it is possible that the file is not yet written. &#x20;\\\\nAsk any question if something is ambiguous or not yet clear.\\\\nBe brief, but never compress away the subject, timing, or causal chain. Define ambiguous technical phrases. use $caveman skill\\\\n\\\\nDo not stage or commit changes. md2 will commit files captured from provider edit tools.\\\",\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"agent-turn-18071b59-1481-489e-b063-913edba96118-user\\\",\\n          \\\"kind\\\": \\\"message\\\",\\n          \\\"role\\\": \\\"user\\\",\\n          \\\"sequence\\\": 1,\\n          \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-08-06T19:02:46.035Z\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n          \\\"details\\\": [],\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"agent-turn-18071b59-1481-489e-b063-913edba96118-event-2\\\",\\n          \\\"kind\\\": \\\"event\\\",\\n          \\\"label\\\": \\\"Reasoning\\\",\\n          \\\"providerItemId\\\": \\\"rs_0e2652d87fdb28cc016a74da5be5348191965a6bbeb3ff1365\\\",\\n          \\\"sequence\\\": 2,\\n          \\\"status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n          \\\"summary\\\": [],\\n          \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-08-06T19:02:50.868Z\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"reasoning\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"agent\\\": \\\"codex\\\",\\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"Using `caveman` for terse updates and final. First inspect target, then every referenced non-agent file, then code paths before editing design doc.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"agent-turn-18071b59-1481-489e-b063-913edba96118-turn-1-assistant-1\\\",\\n          \\\"kind\\\": \\\"message\\\",\\n          \\\"role\\\": \\\"assistant\\\",\\n          \\\"sequence\\\": 3,\\n          \\\"timestamp\