xical selection logic.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Supports element-scoped popup scrolling through `useVirtualizer`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Supports measured row heights; useful when long repository paths wrap.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `scrollToIndex(selectedIndex)` can keep keyboard-highlighted option mounted and visible.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- React 19 supported. Use `useFlushSync: false` per official React 19 guidance. [TanStack React docs](https://tanstack.com/virtual/latest/docs/framework/react/react-virtual)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Current package: `3.14.8`. [npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/%40tanstack/react-virtual)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSuggested setup:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm install @tanstack/react-virtual\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nUse:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Popup `List` as scroll element.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Virtualizer `count = options.length`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Estimated row height plus `measureElement`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Small `overscan`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Effect calling `scrollToIndex(selectedIndex)`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Render only `getVirtualItems()`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPrefer over `react-window`: TanStack integrates better with existing MUI markup and variable-height path rows. `react-window` v2 is more component-prescriptive and recently changed major API.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nImportant: virtualization fixes DOM overload only. Still must stop indexing ignored `node_modules` files and avoid creating 127k option objects while search inactive.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVerification plan accepted: temporary large-index stress test, verify behavior/performance, then remove test. Keep ordinary fast behavior tests only. No changes made.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nChecking React Virtuoso fit against Lexical-controlled selection, MUI markup, variable path rows, React 19, and dependency weight.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`react-virtuoso` good. For this popup, better choice than TanStack Virtual.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWhy:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Flat vertical list: exact Virtuoso sweet spot.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Automatic variable-height measurement. Long paths may wrap; no `estimateSize`/`measureElement` plumbing.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Imperative `scrollIntoView` / `scrollToIndex` fits Lexical keyboard highlight changes. [Scrolling API](https://virtuoso.dev/react-virtuoso/virtuoso/scroll-to-index/)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Custom `Scroller`, `List`, and `Item` components allow MUI integration and correct ARIA roles. [Custom rendering](https://virtuoso.dev/react-virtuoso/virtuoso/customize-rendering/)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- React 19 support maintained. Latest is `4.18.11`. [Changelog](https://virtuoso.dev/react-virtuoso/changelog/), [npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-virtuoso)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRecommendation changed to:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```powershell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm install react-virtuoso\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nImplementation shape:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Extract popup list into own component.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `<Virtuoso data={options} />`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Fixed 320px maximum popup height.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `computeItemKey` from repository path.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `itemContent` renders existing `MarkdownFileSearchOptionItem`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- On Lexical `selectedIndex` change, call `scrollIntoView({ index: selectedIndex })`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Stable custom MUI components declared outside render.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nStill required: Virtuoso reduces DOM nodes, but does not stop creation/filtering of 127k option objects. Excluding ignored files and inactive-query handling remain necessary.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTemporary large-index verification test can be removed afterward, as requested. No changes made.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nImplementing `react-virtuoso` plus source/query fixes. First verify file-index call graph, local/GitHub behavior, Lexical menu contract, and related tests. Temporary stress verification will be removed after proof.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nImpact check:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `readRepositoryFilePaths` has one caller: local `listRepositoryFiles`; replace with Git-aware listing. GitHub/remote paths stay unchanged.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Shared editor behavior unchanged outside file-search popup.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Popup option component keeps selection/focus behavior; new virtual menu owns scrolling/render window.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Existing 150k filesystem test targets helper being removed; remove it. Add only fast mocked Git-boundary and ordinary UI tests.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDependency install still running. Meanwhile design settled: Virtuoso renders visible rows only; selected-index changes call `scrollIntoView`; inactive search produces zero options; local index comes from Git tracked plus nonignored untracked files.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCore changes in place. Running focused tests now; likely risk areas: mocked Git process ordering, Virtuoso jsdom measurement, and Lexical setter typings.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nStress verification passed with 127,035 options: virtualized DOM stayed below 20 rows. Removing temporary stress test now, per request.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nReal local verification: index fell from 127,035 filesystem paths to 1,459 Git-relevant files; zero `node_modules` entries. Running typecheck, auto-fix, lint, then related tests again.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nImplemented fixes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Added `react-virtuoso` virtualization in [markdown_file_search_menu.tsx](C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\janbo\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Documents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dev\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\md2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\